  internal_calculus bonfyre-brief cited: brief type (JSON constrained by CUE) -> CMS source_collection refs filtered by document family -> internet_source twin and retained sha -> newest allowed HTTP 200 ForeignTwin receipt with that sha -> rehashed body -> prose-only term selection over Markdown lines or HTML content text -> brief.json (bf_jsonw), brief.md, receipt.json
  invariant cited mode reads only sources whose CMS family the brief type names; a ref in the same collection with another family is counted as excluded and never read or quoted
  invariant every cited excerpt is the exact byte range recorded with it in a body whose sha256 matches both the CMS row and an allowed HTTP 200 ForeignTwin receipt; a changed body, a refused receipt or an unpinned row becomes a named exception instead of a citation
  invariant a customer inventory is accepted only for the exact subject and scope of the brief and only when it names its grant; criteria read unassessed, needs-inventory or stated-by-customer-inventory and verified is always false
  invariant --expect-sources-digest refuses with exit 4 when the sources a reviewer saw have changed; identical inputs reproduce identical brief bytes
  invariant cited mode makes no network request, publication, spend, WorkGraph admission or CMS write; its receipt states those effects as false
  witness cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/cited_brief_test.sh (make -C cmd/BonfyreBrief test, 2026-10-30) first passed 35 checks on a throwaway CMS, receipts and WorkGraph: unfamiliar brief type, family exclusion, other-namespace refusal, refused-receipt avoidance, exact byte excerpts, HTML head/nav/script exclusion, account-bound identity, inventory subject/scope/grant refusal, stale revision refusal, changed-body exception, no-source refusal, and the brief reaching user:7's account-work Outputs but not user:8's
  witness 2026-10-30 BONFYRE_TEST_LIVE_CMS=~/.bonfyre/estate-local/cms.db adds a read-only pass: all six shipped brief types cite passages from the canonical aurekai and aurekai-migration-briefs-draft source collections; briefs retained under output/migration-briefs-20261030
  witness 2026-10-30 (later) cited_brief_test.sh passes 43 checks (44 with BONFYRE_TEST_LIVE_CMS, all seven shipped types): the shipped cad-ifc, civic-legacy-modernization and document-archive-extraction types read their draft collections by catalogue id on a throwaway CMS, a LICENSE spelling out "GNU Lesser General Public License" or "GNU General Public License" is raised for license-review while MPL, Apache and MIT sources are not, and every shipped-type excerpt is the exact recorded byte range
  witness 2026-10-30 fourteen retained ForeignTwin observations (robots preflight, retained body, receipt under ~/.bonfyre/foreign/receipts, twins open-doc-freecad-readme/-license, open-doc-ezdxf-readme, open-doc-revit-ifc-readme, open-doc-buildingsmart-ids-readme/-user-manual, open-doc-openfn-lightning-readme/-license, open-doc-opencrvs-core-readme, open-doc-ckan-api-guide, open-doc-apache-tika-readme, open-doc-docling-readme, open-doc-unstructured-readme, open-doc-presidio-readme) are internet_source rows 2729-2742 in aurekai-migration-briefs-draft, members of draft source_collection 6196 (civic), 6386 (cad) and 6387 (document); live briefs cad-ifc, civic-legacy-modernization and document-archive-extraction cite all of them
  invariant license-review is raised when a license passage names GPL, LGPL, AGPL or spells out "General Public License"; a project whose README states no license is flagged only through an observed LICENSE row in the same collection
  forbidden_inference a cited FreeCAD, Revit IFC, IDS, OpenFn, OpenCRVS, CKAN, Tika, Docling, Unstructured or Presidio passage -> a validated government workflow, an IFC/IDS fixture that passed, an archive rights decision, a policy effective date, or a PII rule; the sources are README, LICENSE and guide text only
  known_gap no IFC/IDS sample model or .ids fixture, archive metadata/rights record, policy effective-date table or PII rule set has been observed or extracted; the document and CAD briefs cite tool documentation, not transform or test fixtures
  known_gap archived DIGIT-OSS is reference-only and was not observed; the Unstructured README links its license only through a badge, so no license passage is cited for it
  forbidden_inference a cited migration brief -> the customer's system matches the cited documents, the upstream project supports the case, or the migration is safe
  forbidden_inference a proposed range in a cited brief -> a quote, price, invoice or authority to spend
  forbidden_inference a README license mention -> the code's license or rights to adopt it
  known_gap cited mode is not yet wired into Acquisition Brief Studio or the account Program workspace; the brief reaches account Outputs only when a WorkGraph job names it, which the test proves on a throwaway store and the live store has not received
  known_gap the selector is term matching over prose, not semantic extraction; awesome-list READMEs yield list entries rather than migration rules; schema and behavior mappings come only from DatabaseBridge receipts passed with --evidence, not from the brief's own reading
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBrief/src/evidence.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBrief/src/evidence.h
  internal_calculus bonfyre-brief cited --evidence: DatabaseBridge schema-map (seal rechecked) and map-verify (must name a given mapping's digest) -> rule source receipt matched in --receipts -> transformation_evidence in brief.json, a "What a rehearsal measured" section in brief.md, rehearsal_evidence on criteria whose type names that evidence kind, evidence_digest in brief_id and receipt.json
  invariant a map-verify receipt without the mapping it measured, or a mapping that fails its own seal, is refused with exit 3; a rule source without a matching allowed receipt is shown and named evidence-rules-unreceipted, a vendored one evidence-rules-vendored
  invariant evidence never changes a criterion's status or verified flag; without --evidence the brief bytes and identity are unchanged
  witness 2026-10-30 cited_brief_test.sh passes 63 checks: 20 new on transformation evidence built by bonfyre-bridge from its fixtures (column mapping cited to the pgloader rule bytes, diff line, criteria evidence refs, order-independent identity, reproducible bytes, diff-without-mapping and forged-mapping refusal, unreceipted and vendored rule sources named)
  witness 2026-10-30 live sql-erp-migration brief with evidence under output/migration-briefs-20261030/sql-erp-migration-evidence (brief 6e01031247405f795c80f333) cites 6 receipt-verified sources including pgloader docs/ref/sqlite.rst and LICENSE (draft internet_source rows 2743-2744, draft source_collection 6670) and four DatabaseBridge receipts; the live CMS file hash is unchanged by the run
  forbidden_inference a brief's "What a rehearsal measured" section -> the customer's database having been converted or compared; it reports a copy named by sha256
