  witness 2026-10-30 cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/practice_site_test.sh passes against the scratch-built web-address binary: 18 routes answer, site check has no failure, all six brief-type ranges appear verbatim as estimates, the two unbriefed practices read "Priced after the assessment", no bare dollar figure and no stored amount, every practice and hosting-panel page leads to a form that asks its questions, sixteen offer facts are brief-type needs, no client, testimonial, guarantee or internal word appears, the draft is unshared, and a hosting request reaches the inbox with source_panel and site_count; headless Chrome screenshots legacy-*.png in the session scratchpad at 1440 and 390 wide
  forbidden_inference the practice site -> delivered migrations, clients, references or a tested cutover; it presents the method and the deliverables, not a track record
  known_gap the practice site is a draft in a scratch site home; its name (Legacy Migration Practice), its prices and its publication wait for the owner, and the site product refuses the estate's name on an operator site
  known_gap documents/archives and custom applications have no brief type yet, so they carry no range and no cited assessment
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBrief/src/inventory.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBrief/data/hosting-inventory.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/hosting_inventory_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/fixtures/hosting
  internal_calculus bonfyre-brief inventory: site inbox JSON (bonfyre.site.inbox.v1, one request by --reference) + exported listings --export cpanel|interworx|plesk:FILE (WHM listaccts; cPanel API 2 listaddondomains, listpops, MysqlFE listdbs; InterWorx listAccounts, listAllDomains, listEmailBoxes, listMysqlDatabases as API reply or CLI -o json; Plesk XML site get) -> sets of sites, domains, subdomains, mailboxes and databases -> draft bonfyre.hosting-inventory.v1 (bf_jsonw, constrained by hosting-inventory.cue) with per-fact provenance, intake/export disagreements and unparsed answers -> bonfyre-brief cited --inventory
  invariant inventory reads local files only: no panel, server, customer system or network is contacted; under a sandbox that denies the network it writes the same bytes
  invariant an exported listing is read only with --grant naming the owner's authorization (grant_kind export-authorization); intake alone is a customer-statement grant naming the request; a listing a panel reports as failed, or a shape no adapter knows, refuses the whole run with exit 3
  invariant only counts and domain names leave an export; credential fields (crypt_password, ftp_password, anything named pass/secret/token/crypt) are counted and never copied; panel limits (maxpop, maxsql) are never read as counts; cPanel's Main Account row is not a mailbox
  invariant where a listing speaks to a fact its value is used and a differing answer is kept as a disagreement; cited reads a criterion disputed when any need is disagreed, read-from-exported-listing when every need came from an export, and never verified; inventories without provenance read exactly as before
  witness 2026-10-31 cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/hosting_inventory_test.sh (make -C cmd/BonfyreBrief test) passes 47 checks on fixtures shaped by the panels' documented sample outputs (tests/fixtures/hosting/sources.json names each page, twin and sha256): cPanel 3 sites/4 mailboxes/3 databases with the Main Account row and limits excluded, InterWorx 3 sites/1 subdomain/4 mailboxes/3 databases with four password hashes dropped, Plesk 2 sites/3 domains with the error result counted and ftp_password dropped, intake-only customer-statement grant with "about four" left out and named, seven refusals, reproducible bytes, CUE vet of every inventory and refusal of a forged grant_kind, a no-network sandbox run, and briefs over each inventory with disputed/read-from-exported-listing/stated statuses, scaled estimate, human-worded exceptions and a sources-digest replay to identical bytes
  witness 2026-10-31 with BONFYRE_TEST_WEB_BINARY=cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/bonfyre-web-address the same test (48 checks) posts the hosting form of the practice draft in a throwaway site home, reads its own site inbox --json, and turns that request plus the cPanel fixtures into an inventory and brief with no disagreement; with BONFYRE_TEST_LIVE_CMS the shipped hosting brief over the cPanel fixture inventory reads all five receipt-verified hosting documents read-only (CMS hash unchanged), retained under output/migration-briefs-20261030/hosting-account-acquisition-fixture-inventory (brief fc08a75aca3ee1b77869512b)
  witness 2026-10-31 eleven ForeignTwin observations of panel API documentation (open-doc-cpanel-whm-listaccts-md, open-doc-cpanel-api2-email-listpops, open-doc-cpanel-api2-mysqlfe-listdbs, open-doc-cpanel-api2-addondomain-list, open-doc-cpanel-api-llms-index, open-doc-cpanel-uapi-introduction, open-doc-interworx-api-siteworx-listaccounts, open-doc-interworx-api-siteworx-email-box, open-doc-interworx-api-siteworx-mysql-db, open-doc-plesk-xml-site-get, open-doc-plesk-rest-domains) under ~/.bonfyre/foreign/receipts; they ground the fixture shapes and are not CMS rows or brief citations
  forbidden_inference a hosting inventory read from an exported listing -> the live server holds that account today, the listing is complete, or the move is safe; it is the export the owner handed over, unverified against the server
  forbidden_inference an inventory adapter passing on fixtures -> it reads a real panel's export correctly; fixtures follow documented samples, and no real cPanel, InterWorx or Plesk export has been read
  known_gap no real exported listing from any panel has been read; Plesk is adapted only for the XML site get packet (no mail or database listing, no REST /api/v2 bodies, whose reference is served only by a running server); cPanel UAPI list_pops/list_databases pages were not found, so the API 2 equivalents are read; DNS zones, TTLs, backups, PHP versions and mail sizes are not read from exports
  known_gap no 3-site pilot, compatibility report, staged copy, browser/mail/DB proof or reversible cutover plan exists; the inventory is a draft nobody has reviewed with a customer, and no customer system was touched

architecture cmd-c-l-i
  canonical_name BonfyreCLI
  family command
  domain Command / CLI
  semantic_question What does the BonfyreCLI capability organ realize, and by what contract?
  purpose The bonfyre front door: a start screen for a first-time user, commands grouped by what a person wants to do, and plain errors that point at the right command. It routes to organs; it owns none of their effects.
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreCLI
  internal_calculus bonfyre binary: one route table carrying goal section and audience tier (start, everyday, lab)
  invariant bare bonfyre and bonfyre help print the same short start screen; every everyday and start command is reachable from it
  invariant lab kernels, internals and discovered local builds are hidden from list and search unless --all; list --json always carries every route with its tier
  invariant a discovered binary is a command only when its name is lowercase words joined by '-'; backup, archive and patched copies are never listed or dispatched
  invariant an unknown command exits 1 with the closest spellings, then commands whose purpose names the word; only the runtime's own verbs fall through to bonfyre-runtime
  invariant every command shown to people answers --help, -h and help with usage on stdout, nothing on stderr, exit 0 and no file created (lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_help.h)
  forbidden_inference the command exists -> its effect is authorized (read-only, but scope still applies)
  forbidden_inference a command on the start screen or in the everyday tier -> that it is production-ready for every input, or that its organ's maturity is higher than its own atlas entry
  forbidden_inference a passing help contract -> that the command's real work succeeds; help is checked without any store, model or device
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCLI/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCLI/tests/front_door.test.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCLI/tests/help_contract.test.mjs
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_help.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreCLI/tests/front_door.test.mjs checks the start screen, tier coverage, lab hiding and --all, typo and goal-word suggestions with exit 1, subcommand usage, and that dotted backup binaries are neither listed nor run
  witness cmd/BonfyreCLI/tests/help_contract.test.mjs runs --help, -h and help against every built start and everyday organ with an empty HOME and fails on non-zero exit, stderr output or any created file; 68 of 68 passed on 2026-10-16
  witness cmd/BonfyreCLI/tests/public_command_contract.mjs keeps the declared 91-command public ABI unchanged
  witness cmd/BonfyreCLI/tests/vectors/command_behavior.json + packs/no-simulation/command-behavior-20261029.tsv: behavior vectors on small real fixtures in fresh temp dirs, replayed by make -C tests/vectors check (2026-10-29): command.precision=pass,command.self=pass,command.status=pass
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
  known_gap the installed bonfyre-auth predates the help contract because a live service runs it; it opens its store on --help until it is reinstalled with its reviewed source
  known_gap subcommand help (bonfyre site new --help and similar) is not yet covered by the contract; only the organ's first argument is
  known_gap the npm @aurekai/runtime package also installs a program named bonfyre (akai.mjs); which one a person gets depends on PATH order

architecture cmd-c-m-s
  canonical_name BonfyreCMS
  family command
  domain Surface / CMS
  semantic_question What does the BonfyreCMS capability organ realize, and by what contract?
  purpose Command-surface organ realizing the Publication capability. A first-class Bonfyre capability, advertised and composable, not a script.
  maturity implemented
  command BonfyreCMS
  internal_calculus bonfyre-cms binary
  invariant the first and second CLI verbs resolve once through sorted native command tables; their handlers retain argument, store, authority, output and return-code semantics
  forbidden_inference the command exists -> its effect is authorized (Authority gates the commit)
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/ann_index.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/ann_index.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/bench_metrics.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/bench_metrics.h
  witness packs/no-simulation/command-evidence-20261010.tsv
  invariant an entry update is as large as its fields allow and every value in it is quoted by SQLite; a value cannot end the statement or reach another column
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/large_update_test.sh updates a 24,000-character field full of quotes, backslashes and newlines and reads back exactly what was sent, shows a hostile status value is stored as words, and that another namespace or an emptied required field leaves the row as it was
  invariant a guarded CLI entry update compares its declared string field and namespace in the same SQL update; a failed condition leaves both content and edit history unchanged
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/conditional_update.test.mjs races two native writers, admits one, refuses stale and wrong-namespace writes, and reads a guarded file-body update back exactly
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/cms_subcommand_dispatch.test.mjs checks sorted second-verb vocabulary, all 65 call sites, known and unknown dispatch, output and exit codes
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
  known_gap operator command.cms quality-proven on a real input in the command workload of 2026-10-10 (receipt rcpt-ec0901253288b794848d), one run on one input; realizes Publication; deeper development toward the BonfyreFS level (WiringSpec consumes/produces, full contract) is ongoing
  known_gap publication_rss_tag returned entity-encoded text as if it were text. Decoding is now done in the promoter after identity is taken, and `publication repair-entities` rewrites rows promoted before the fix in place, rebuilding the family and ANN indexes once inside the same transaction and emitting the repaired titles for re-embedding.
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/nutrition_reference_web.test.mjs saves the full 46415-byte reference formulation through the native CMS form into its private namespace
  invariant decoded field strings remain bounded to 64 KiB inside the existing 1 MiB CMS request limit, with per-type validation and namespace checks unchanged
  invariant entry page-write validates one bounded page aggregate and its explicit namespace, checks the expected page identity under BEGIN IMMEDIATE, and commits typed page rows, fragments and operation history together; failed writes discard queued hooks and emit no publication notifications
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/page_write.test.mjs checks storage and operation-history rollback, namespace and stale-identity refusal, malformed and oversized input, concurrent whole-page replacements, hook reads after commit, and explicit committed status when notification delivery fails
  known_gap page-write hooks and publication notifications run after commit without a durable outbox; process failure can interrupt delivery even when the content transaction committed
  invariant page-write replacement checks the caller-reviewed full page-and-fragment digest and page identity inside the owner transaction; concurrent stale replacements refuse rather than last-writer-wins
  forbidden_inference an atomic CMS page transaction -> durable external effects, successful notification delivery or verified public deployment
