  witness 2026-09-26 the core application could not be compiled at all and nothing said so. frappe ships new-doctype-1 and new-doctype-2, two scaffolds whose fields carry a label and no fieldname, and taking a copy of that absent name killed the process partway through phase 7. The smaller applications compiled cleanly and hid it: every other Frappe app depends on frappe, so the one that mattered most was the one that crashed
  witness 2026-09-26 with a field the DocType never named skipped rather than copied, frappe compiles: 271 DocTypes, 271 rule universes, all twelve phases. Nine applications now compile end to end -- crm, drive, erpnext, frappe, helpdesk, hrms, insights, lms, wiki -- for 1,152 DocTypes in total
  witness 2026-09-26 two emitters added in the same pass: --emit-surface-programs writes the layout as JSON, --emit-surface-db writes it into a store the composer queries, and a recompile replaces that application's rows rather than accumulating a second version of each DocType
  invariant a DocType the compiler cannot name yields no rule universe and is named as skipped, and the universe array is left dense rather than holding a gap the theorem checks would dereference
  known_gap responds to --help (live); realizes FrappeCompilerCapability; deeper development toward the BonfyreFS level (WiringSpec consumes/produces, full contract) is ongoing
  known_gap bonfyre_erpnext, the estate's own overlay application, still exits non-zero and the cause has not been diagnosed
