  invariant file hashing publishes a digest only after reaching EOF without a stream error and closing successfully; open, read and close failure return an empty digest and preserve the error
  invariant file and dedup commands use the shared file hasher; a file hash failure aborts a duplicate scan before any duplicate report is printed
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/sha256_file_test.c checks empty, abc and buffer-boundary vectors, missing paths, directory reads, immediate and partial stream errors, close failure and stream cleanup; the earlier primitive fails nine of eighteen checks
  witness cmd/BonfyreHash/tests/file.test.mjs compares eleven file sizes on both backends against an independent digest, checks complete duplicate pairs, refuses directory and absent inputs and injects a partial read failure into file and dedup commands
  forbidden_inference a successful file hash -> a stable snapshot or permission to remove a duplicate; concurrent changes and directory enumeration completeness are not established by this reader
  known_gap static consumers require rebuilding to receive shared primitive changes; Hash, Fabric, Ingest and Compress are rebuilt and installed, not every existing consumer binary
