  invariant --type document picks its reader from the bytes first (a %PDF signature is PDF), then the source-declared media type given as --mime, then the extension, then a head sniff; HTML is read as text with markup dropped, text media are normalized as text, and a declared PDF without PDF bytes is refused rather than relabelled
