  command context-compile ... [--task REF] [--revision REV] binds the compiled context to one task and source revision and prints the sha256 of every body and of the written context
  command context-verify --receipt COMPILE.json --bodies DIR --context FILE [--task REF] [--revision REV] admits a compiled context as a handoff only while every listed body and the context still hash as compiled, no body appeared or vanished, every required sentence is still in the context, and the task and revision match; prints bonfyre.context.handoff.v1 through bf_jsonw
  invariant a handoff is refused, never substituted, when the context, any body or the body set changed since compilation, or when it was bound to another task or revision or to none
  invariant a handoff needs at least one required sentence; a context with no witness is not a verified handoff
  invariant the handoff's token counts are tokenizer counts and say so (token_basis tokenizer_count_not_provider_usage); they are never provider usage or billed tokens
  forbidden_inference a verified handoff -> the agent consumed it, or that it is sufficient context for the task
  forbidden_inference a smaller tokenizer count -> fewer provider tokens, lower cost or equal answer quality
  witness cmd/BonfyreKVCache/tests/context_contract.sh (2026-10-30): a context bound to task and revision verifies; another task, another revision, an unbound receipt, a witness-free context, an edited context, an edited body, a new body and a removed body are each refused with the reason
