architecture cmd-meter
  canonical_name BonfyreMeter
  family command
  domain Command / Meter
  semantic_question What does the BonfyreMeter capability organ realize, and by what contract?
  purpose Own admitted provider rates and evidenced physical-attempt usage; expose bounded native rate and retained-event packets to scoped Fabric execution without a parallel price or usage store
  maturity implemented
  command BonfyreMeter
  internal_calculus bonfyre-meter binary
  forbidden_inference a meter key or physical-attempt receipt -> account execution authority, an invoice, or an admitted payment
  forbidden_inference no applicable admitted rate -> zero cost or a known maximum price
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMeter/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMeter/src/meter_packet.h
  source_path integrations/mcp/native_meter.mjs
  command quote-packet --db ABS --provider ID --op OP --at UTC returns one MessagePack v1 packet with the exact applicable admitted unit rate or explicit unknown pricing; the read does not create an absent store
  command record-packet --db ABS --key SUBJECT --op OP --provider ID --bytes N --duration MS --receipt REF --attempt-ref REF --realization-ref REF --at UTC retains the existing evidenced physical-attempt owner event and returns its exact readback
  command event-packet --db ABS --key SUBJECT --attempt-ref REF reads only that retained key and physical-attempt identity
  invariant the account owner admits execution before calling Meter; adapter keys carry its native subject and do not grant scope
  invariant exact physical-attempt replay retains the original event and rate; a changed account, receipt, realization, byte count, duration, provider, operation, or timestamp under that identity is refused
  invariant priced usage names its retained native rate and cost; unknown pricing never supplies a fabricated rate or estimate, and corrupt or mismatched evidence is unavailable
  invariant a transport or readback failure after record may follow a committed event; retry the same frozen attempt metadata without rerunning model execution
  witness packs/no-simulation/command-evidence-20261010.tsv
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/native_meter.test.mjs compiles the actual native owner and proves exact packet binding, measured event readback, account and attempt conflicts, replay identity, admitted unit-rate arithmetic, retained event-time pricing, and unavailable evidence
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/vectors/command_behavior.json + packs/no-simulation/command-behavior-20261029.tsv: behavior vectors on small real fixtures in fresh temp dirs, replayed by make -C tests/vectors check (2026-10-29): command.meter=pass
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
  known_gap priced events require rates actually admitted by the native operator; the packet adapter does not admit customer rates, infer token counts, estimate maximum cost, create invoices, or settle payments
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMeter/src/meter_tokens.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/token_evidence_test.sh compares complete priced and unpriced work-token reports, including shared sessions, cross-account refusal, provider isolation and a store without the session index; the selected event IDs retain report input order
  command token-import --db METER --subject ACCOUNT --source RECONCILED_EVENTS_CSV records each row of a reconciled Claude Code / Codex usage export as one model.tokens physical-attempt event in the existing events table: provider, session, execution, request, message, turn, model, effort, uncached/cached/cache-write/output/reasoning counters, counter basis, row digest and file digest; all-or-nothing
  command token-usage --db METER --subject ACCOUNT [--work-db WORK_INDEX --scope SCOPE] reads token counters by provider and model, separates inherited cumulative snapshots from additive counts, values only through admitted dated per-token rates, and counts sessions that map exactly to a task, are named but refused, or stay unmapped
  command work-tokens --db METER --work-db WORK_INDEX --subject ACCOUNT --scope SCOPE --mission TASK reads one task's token evidence through the provider session keys the Work index carries, including failed runs, and refuses another account's task
  invariant a token row's identity is the provider's own request and message id (Claude) or, where the provider gives none (Codex token_count), its coordinates, row digest and ordinal among byte-identical rows; an identical row replays, a changed one under the same identity refuses the whole export
  invariant the transcript path and text never enter the store; only derived counters, ids and digests do
  invariant token counters attribute to a task only when exactly one indexed task and one provider name the session, for the same account key; nothing is joined by time, title or proximity
  invariant unreported counters stay null (Claude reasoning), and a token event with any reported dimension lacking an admitted rate in effect at the attempt time stays unvalued
  forbidden_inference a provisional token valuation -> what the account was charged, invoiced or paid; subscription plans and credits are not per-token prices
  forbidden_inference a session with token evidence but no exact Work key -> usage of any particular task
  forbidden_inference a Codex first cumulative snapshot -> new usage in that session; it may carry inherited parent history and is reported apart, never added or valued
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/token_evidence_test.sh (make test-token-evidence, 2026-10-30): idempotent replay, identical Codex deltas kept apart, repeated request id with changed counters refusing the whole export, cross-account replay refused, inconsistent counters, unknown basis and foreign headers refused, two workers on one task with a failed run recovered, a shared session refused, another account's task refused, effective-dated partial valuation 0.018300 USD with unknown cache-write rate, keyless index refused
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/token_archive_witness.sh replays the owner's private reconciled export in a throwaway store (2026-10-30): 93,512 rows, 18,224,040,007 tokens (codex 11,142,839,269 / claude 7,081,200,738 matching the export summary), 7,860,929 in 297 inherited snapshots, replay 0 new, no price without an admitted rate; SKIP where the export is absent
  witness 2026-10-30 against a copy of user:19's operator and Fabric stores indexed by the rebuilt Queue: 286 sessions, 62 map exactly to a task, 0 named-but-refused, 224 unmapped; 50 tasks carry token evidence
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMeter/src/meter_context.h
  command context-compare --db METER --work-db WORK_INDEX --subject ACCOUNT --scope SCOPE --mission TASK --baseline-run RUN --compact-run RUN --handoff CONTEXT_VERIFY.json puts two runs of one Work item side by side in provider counter classes (uncached, cached, cache-write, output, reasoning, expensive new input = uncached + cache-write), with per-side provisional valuation at admitted rates in effect at each attempt and deltas only for a comparable pair; read-only
  invariant both sides are runs of the same Work item in the requested account and scope, each with a provider session that maps to that task alone and has imported usage under the same account key; same run, shared session, keyless run, run without usage, run of another task, another account and a keyless index are refused with no output
  invariant the handoff must be a PASS bonfyre.context.handoff.v1 receipt verified for the same task; a compile receipt, a refused handoff or one for another task is refused
  invariant deltas are printed only for the same provider and a single same model on both sides with no inherited cumulative snapshot; otherwise the sides are shown and comparable names why not
  invariant side counters are additive rows; snapshot rows and tokens are shown apart; a side's valuation is printed only when every record has admitted rates, and the delta only when both sides do
  forbidden_inference a context-compare delta -> the compact handoff caused it; the handoff binding is declared by the caller, not observed at launch
  forbidden_inference handoff_binding recorded_by_claimed_workgraph_attempt_not_consumption_observed -> the agent read the handoff; it means the claimed attempt named that receipt when it attested its session
  invariant where the account Work index carries handoff_ref (runs projected from attested WorkGraph attempts), the record decides: a baseline run that recorded this handoff and a compact run that recorded a different one are both refused, and a compact run that recorded it prints handoff_binding recorded_by_claimed_workgraph_attempt_not_consumption_observed
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/context_compare_test.sh governed section (make test-context-compare, 2026-10-30): one native WorkGraph node run twice through the real Queue CLI (attempt 1 attested claude sess-base, failed transient; attempt 2 attested claude sess-compact with the handoff digest, acked), indexed by account-work, compared by Meter: recorded binding, comparable yes, expensive-new-input delta -3,100, provisional valuation delta -0.187125 USD, outcome run_state_differs; a session reused for a second attempt, a baseline that recorded the handoff and a compact run that recorded another handoff are refused with their reasons
  forbidden_inference equal run state -> equal answer quality; quality_acceptance is reported as not_measured
  forbidden_inference fewer cached-input tokens -> a saving of the same size; cache reads and new input are different price classes
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/context_compare_test.sh (make test-context-compare, 2026-10-30): comparable Claude pair gives expensive-new-input delta -3,100 and provisional valuation delta -0.187125 USD at rates effective before the runs while a later-dated rate is ignored; missing cache-write rate leaves both sides and the delta unknown; provider, model and snapshot mismatches print sides without deltas; nine refusals leave no output; the read writes nothing
  witness 2026-10-30 on copies of the live meter store and account-work index: a real handoff verified for account-fabric-0517e123c84a429aa6a15530 and its two completed Codex runs read back additive counters (78,143 vs 108,017 uncached) with comparable no_inherited_snapshot_present, because each Codex session's first counter is a cumulative snapshot; 47 tasks carry Codex token evidence, 3 carry Claude evidence and none has two Claude runs
  known_gap no run has yet been executed on a verified compact handoff, so no real before/after measurement exists; producing one needs equivalent safe tasks run by the agents, which this build did not do (no provider calls)
  known_gap every Codex session opens with a first cumulative snapshot, so Codex pairs are incomparable until the launcher records that a session was fresh rather than forked
  known_gap the comparison is a Meter read; the account Workboard and Finance surfaces do not show it
  witness 2026-10-30 managed ~/.bonfyre/bin/bonfyre-meter promoted through scripts/organ_drift.sh --sync --only, byte-identical to the checkout build (sha256 cce847ee48d31d60...), built -Oz with dead stripping at 88,784 bytes (was 90,576)
  known_gap no per-token rate is admitted: the export's API-equivalent USD is a third-party estimate without per-token evidence, so all 93,215 additive token events remain unvalued and nothing about charges, plan quota or credits is known
  known_gap 224 of 286 sessions (interactive Claude Code and Codex sessions) have no exact Work key; operator API runs carry response ids the export does not include, so those runs stay unmetered here
  known_gap exact eligible single-run Meter counters reach the account Workboard index and task provenance; unmatched or ambiguous sessions remain unreported, Finance/Workbook continuations do not yet show the evidence, and no editable task forecast exists

