  invariant POST /bonfyre/lease?ttl=S[&prefer=a,b] loads if needed and pins the resident model: while any lease is live the front neither promotes nor unloads it; renew= extends, release= ends, and ttl is capped at 3600 s so a crashed caller holds memory for one ttl at most
  invariant a preference swaps the resident model only when no lease holds it and no request is open; otherwise the lease is on the resident model and says preferred:false
  forbidden_inference a lease was granted -> the preferred model answered; the grant names model_path and whether the preference was met
  known_gap with no preference the front still ranks by file size; a program's preferred model is passed by the caller (--model or BONFYRE_LOCAL_MODEL_PREFER), not yet chosen from measured per-program results
  known_gap admission prices memory only: download and staging disk, swap growth and output size are not part of the grant

architecture cmd-mo-q
  canonical_name BonfyreMoQ
  family command
  domain Command / MoQ
  semantic_question What does the BonfyreMoQ capability organ realize, and by what contract?
  purpose Live-object protocol utility: a clearly labelled TCP compatibility frame relay plus draft-ietf-moq-transport-21 SETUP/SUBSCRIBE encoders and a native-QUIC paired-control/request path. The relay is not MOQT; native QUIC validates paired SETUP streams and rejects an unleased or revoked SUBSCRIBE. A separate MediaDelivery owner can project an opaque type-0 authorization token into SUBSCRIBE; the listener rechecks the exact, time-bounded MOQT lease and matching representation before emitting control-only SUBSCRIBE_OK.
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreMoQ
  internal_calculus draft-ietf-moq-transport-21 SETUP/SUBSCRIBE: MOQT 1..9 byte vi64 type/request/namespace/track fields plus u16 message body length -> protocol-owned native QUIC raw uni control stream + raw bidi request stream under ALPN moqt-21 and DATAGRAM transport parameters; compatibility relay retains an independent TCP frame format
  forbidden_inference the command exists -> its effect is authorized (read-only, but scope still applies)
  forbidden_inference a TCP frame relay -> a MOQT session or interoperable live-object transport
  forbidden_inference a valid MOQT wire request -> a subscribed track, authority, or transport lease
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMoQ/src/main.c
  source_path lib/libquic-transport/include/bf_quic.h
  source_path lib/libquic-transport/bf_quic.c
  witness packs/no-simulation/command-evidence-20261010.tsv
  witness cmd/BonfyreMoQ/tests/moqt_wire_test.sh verifies draft-21 SUBSCRIBE and native-QUIC SETUP frames, MOQT ALPN declaration and malformed-name/path refusal
  witness cmd/BonfyreMoQ/tests/moqt_native_session_test.sh proves a local TLS/QUIC handshake under moqt-21, DATAGRAM-enabled raw profile, complete client SETUP on a unidirectional control stream, paired server SETUP parsing before client SUBSCRIBE, and REQUEST_ERROR UNAUTHORIZED on the same bidirectional request stream without a TransportLease/Authority projection; it explicitly records refusal rather than authorization or SUBSCRIBE_OK
  witness cmd/BonfyreMoQ/tests/moqt_leased_session_test.sh proves an actual native MediaDelivery lease is carried as a draft-21 AUTHORIZATION TOKEN parameter, rechecked by the MOQT listener for moqt protocol and matching representation, and yields SUBSCRIBE_OK with no media objects
  witness cmd/BonfyreMoQ/results/2026-09-11-native-quic-moqt-session.json records the executed loopback native-QUIC result and its explicit non-proof frontier
  witness cmd/BonfyreMoQ/tests/vectors/command_behavior.json + packs/no-simulation/command-behavior-20261029.tsv: behavior vectors on small real fixtures in fresh temp dirs, replayed by make -C tests/vectors check (2026-10-29): command.moq=pass
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
  known_gap the native path now executes paired control/request streams, draft-21 AUTHORIZATION TOKEN serialization, a revocation-aware MediaDelivery lease recheck and SUBSCRIBE_OK parsing. It still needs persistent session lifetime, full parameter semantics, actual object/datagram forwarding, relay aggregation, token rotation/replay policy, delivery receipts and WebTransport; a control-only subscription is intentionally not advertised as media delivery or interoperable relay service.

