architecture cmd-runtime
  canonical_name BonfyreRuntime
  family command
  domain Command / Runtime
  semantic_question What does the BonfyreRuntime capability organ realize, and by what contract?
  purpose Command-surface organ realizing the RuntimeCapability capability. A first-class Bonfyre capability, advertised and composable, not a script.
  maturity implemented
  command BonfyreRuntime
  internal_calculus bonfyre-runtime binary
  internal_calculus branch: one live guest on a pipe -> candidate action sequences run in forks of the guest -> an external ranker scores where each lands -> one step committed to the command log
  invariant branch holds candidate state apart from Actual: a fork never moves the guest, and only a committed step is written to the log
  invariant branch takes no score from a ranker that exited non-zero or returned the wrong count; it stops rather than guess
  forbidden_inference the command exists -> its effect is authorized (read-only, but scope still applies)
  forbidden_inference a branch that ranked best -> a committed effect, or proof the guest is deterministic; branch assumes determinism and exact forks and checks neither
  source_path cmd/BonfyreRuntime/src/main.c
  witness packs/no-simulation/command-evidence-20261010.tsv
  witness cmd/BonfyreRuntime/tests/dispatch_test.sh branch drives a counter guest to its goal committing only the higher-ranked step, and stops on a ranker that exits non-zero
  witness 2026-10-03 packs/doom-guest/measured-witness.yaff branch held a foreign guest through 577 decisions and 88281 forks; replaying the committed log in a fresh process reached the same end state
  witness cmd/BonfyreRuntime/tests/vectors/command_behavior.json + packs/no-simulation/command-behavior-20261029.tsv: behavior vectors on small real fixtures in fresh temp dirs, replayed by make -C tests/vectors check (2026-10-29): command.doctor=pass,command.runtime=pass
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
