architecture cmd-swarm
  canonical_name BonfyreSwarm
  family command
  domain Command / Swarm
  semantic_question Which exact owner-admitted artifact may this recipient receive, and what did the peer actually confirm?
  purpose BonfyreSwarm carries one account/output-owner-admitted artifact over bounded IPv4 loopback. scoped-seed and scoped-fetch bind scope, recipient, transfer ID, exact SHA-256, byte length and expiry to fresh challenge proofs using the existing native keyed BLAKE2b owner. Native receivers publish verified bytes without overwriting existing files and record receipt state in the existing Swarm index. transfer-capabilities advertises the implemented boundary.
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreSwarm
  internal_calculus bonfyre-swarm binary
  forbidden_inference transport key possession, a scope hash, a recipient hash or a catalogue entry -> account/output/recipient authority
  forbidden_inference loopback transfer receipt or receiver acknowledgement -> remote encrypted transport, independent storage attestation, peer discovery or distributed model execution
  forbidden_inference legacy seed/fetch or a connected peer -> admission to customer activity or private output access
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSwarm/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSwarm/src/scoped_transfer.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSwarm/Makefile
  source_path integrations/mcp/fabric_output_transfer.mjs
  invariant explicit local output verification requires current native read and write access, the task initiating actor and exact destination, and the immutable artifact descriptor supplied by the output owner
  invariant local verification starts two loopback native peers only on an explicit action; customer packets cannot supply a file path, digest, host, transport key or recipient grant
  invariant an exclusive retained request claim and scoped Fabric receipt make exact retries observational; an uncertain transfer is never silently retransmitted
  invariant a verified local result confirms both native receipts and received byte identity; its temporary received copy and transport key are removed, and no remote delivery or pairing claim is made
  witness cmd/BonfyreSwarm/tests/scoped_transfer_test.c
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_output_transfer.test.mjs exercises actual native peers against a retained scoped Fabric output, current account authority, exact replay across restart, revocation before receiver dispatch, owner shutdown, and unavailable evidence
  witness packs/no-simulation/command-evidence-20261010.tsv
  witness cmd/BonfyreSwarm/tests/vectors/command_behavior.json + packs/no-simulation/command-behavior-20261029.tsv: behavior vectors on small real fixtures in fresh temp dirs, replayed by make -C tests/vectors check (2026-10-29): command.swarm=pass
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
  known_gap scoped transfer is limited to one 64 MiB artifact, one use per direction in its owner-selected index and 300 seconds; the initiating owner must authorize account, recipient and immutable output before provisioning the local key. Receipt states preserve stored_unconfirmed when final confirmation is lost. Remote discovery, an encrypted remote carrier and distributed inference are unavailable. Legacy seed is loopback only and refuses the former gate-key extension rather than disclosing a credential. Historical command.swarm receipt rcpt-7e167760ae47c346d9cc remains a separate one-input witness.

