  known_gap document removal requires the caller to enumerate every indexed passage ID; no automatic source-to-passage removal or secure erasure is claimed
  source_lineage the 91-command capability surface
  known_gap operator command.vec quality-proven on a real input in the command workload of 2026-10-10 (receipt rcpt-3c3294992d6efa492012), one run on one input; realizes SID; deeper development toward the BonfyreFS level (WiringSpec consumes/produces, full contract) is ongoing
  known_gap search held its query in a VEC_DIMS buffer of 384 floats. VEC_DIMS is the width `init` creates a store at, not the width every store has, so a 768-dimension query against a 768-dimension store was cut to 384 floats and bound against a float[768] column: the query and the store described different vectors and the result was reported as a search. The exact path failed the other way, skipping every row whose width differed and returning an empty result that read as "nothing is similar". Both now read the store's width from its own first vector and refuse a mismatch by name.
  known_gap result text was printed into JSON unescaped, so the output stopped being JSON the first time an embedded headline contained a quote. Escaped through bf_lex on both search paths.

