architecture mcp-recursive-native-overlay
  canonical_name McpRecursiveNativeOverlay
  family commands
  domain MCP / Recursive owner-backed transport
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can the recursive MCP additions run in Bun while preserving the rich mesh's existing tools, receipts, authority gates, resources, prompts and auxiliary HTTP routes?
  node_types McpTool
  node_types McpResource
  node_types CallReceipt
  state_types admitted
  state_types refused
  internal_calculus authenticated Bun gateway -> local Matrix/foreign/CMS/surface/circuit owner, 38 native rich handlers including CUE-gated Oracle operations, bounded artifacts, foreign observation, and finance pricing, or exact project node for 15 rich verbs and 9 additional project verbs
  invariant one CUE policy lists 24 project-owned forwarded names; their current schemas replace stale mesh declarations only when the project owner advertises them, and absent owner calls refuse without a Python substitute
  invariant native calls append to the existing mesh SQLite call/event ledger with one authenticated transport
  invariant native subprocess and carrier outputs are bounded in memory while their streams are drained; protocol fetch does not follow redirects into an unadmitted host
  invariant native receipts redact credential and approval tokens and record patch digests rather than raw patch bodies while retaining trace, tool, state and duration
  invariant project-node effect verbs retain that node's own admission boundary; the overlay never upgrades a listed tool or joined read to authority
  invariant a CMS measurement runner is a bare file declaration; only a present native Bun runner may be invoked, and QUERY/PURE admission precedes execution
  invariant Oracle units, profiles, and deep-flow filenames are authored once in CUE; unknown names never reach an argv slot, and deep flows force external writes and live apply off
  invariant artifact reads resolve real paths beneath the output root and bound returned bytes; artifact search does not traverse symlinks
  invariant native foreign discovery and finance-price writes invoke their existing C owners with validated argv and pinned shared stores; their MCP presence does not imply observation truth or sale authority
  invariant the DecisionPlane tool receives a finite exact shortlist from the current live tool catalogue, admits only tools explicitly annotated read-only, requires an information-policy class before any hosted call, and never invokes its suggested tool
  invariant the decision tool is not advertised as read-only because an explicit execution can send public intent to a hosted model; its ledger stores intent digest and byte count instead of raw intent text
  forbidden_inference native source parity or an owner schema -> live deployment, adoption, effect authority, or a true external observation
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_overlay.cue
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_overlay.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreDecision/frontier-adapters.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_overlay_tools.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/bounded_pipe.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/carriers_contract.json
  source_path mcp/rich-catalog.json
  source_path mcp/rich-native-tools.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/promote_recursive_gateway.sh
  source_path integrations/mcp/systemd/bonfyre-mcp-gateway.service.d/recursive-closure.conf
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_overlay.test.mjs proves owner CLI coordinates, foreign receipt/body retention, bounded circuit authority, schema forwarding, resources, trace ledger, bearer and origin gates
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_overlay.test.mjs proves all five rich resource bindings, prompt and catalog parity, native delta/events/metrics, and refusal when the project owner is absent
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_overlay.test.mjs proves a planned and diagnostic typed read-only tool proposal, effecting-tool refusal, and private hosted-state refusal through the authenticated gateway
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_overlay_smoke.mjs checks the promoted MCP entrypoint's tools, resources, prompts and native auxiliary routes
  witness mcp/tests/rich-native-tools.test.mjs proves bounded native Atlas, calls, deltas, measurements, finance book, carrier projection, Oracle allowlists, output-root artifact confinement, owner-effect argv, and allowlisted runtime operations
  known_gap source-level native parity is tested but the deployment promotion has not run here; this entry does not certify the live Oracle or OAuth edge

architecture project-delta-producer
  canonical_name ProjectDeltaProducer
  family commands
  domain MCP / Local project delta observation
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can a local Git snapshot be journaled and delivered to the existing native MCP delta lane without a Python watcher or false delivery acknowledgement?
  node_types ProjectSnapshot
  node_types DeltaJournalEntry
  state_types observed
  state_types pending
  state_types delivered
  internal_calculus four Git reads with branch/upstream parsed from the porcelain-v2 NUL status -> SHA-256 of that exact status -> one local journal entry per newly observed hash -> bounded latest pending HTTP delivery
  invariant the journal is appended before every first publish attempt; a failed POST remains pending and retries on an unchanged poll without another journal entry
  invariant a newer observed hash replaces the one pending remote delivery while the local journal retains both observations; the watcher does not infer historical remote completeness
  invariant transport failures back off from the normal 750-millisecond poll to at most 30 seconds while every poll still observes and journals Git state; new observations do not bypass the retry deadline and a successful POST resets it
  invariant the producer uses the existing authenticated /internal/delta gateway and preserves branch, upstream, head, working/staged status counts and the first 50 path samples
  invariant Git subprocesses inherit the watcher environment except GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, so a persistent read observer does not request optional index refresh locks
  invariant a failed, timed-out or over-16-MiB Git read refuses the snapshot; only rev-parse HEAD in a porcelain-confirmed unborn repository may retain the legacy HEAD marker
  invariant gateway response bodies are never logged and are cancelled above 64 KiB before the watcher considers a delivery successful
  forbidden_inference a journaled snapshot or a failed or ambiguous HTTP attempt -> remote delta delivery, source truth, or authorization to mutate the project
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_delta_watcher.mjs
  source_path deploy/launchd/com.bonfyre.project-delta-watcher.plist
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_delta_cutover.json records the Python process exit, unchanged non-program LaunchAgent configuration and restarted Bun PID; the upstream tunnel remains unloaded and delivery unverified
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_delta_benchmark.meta.json records exact fixture parity and five-to-four Git process reduction; noisy Hyperfine timings do not certify a dependable speedup
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_delta_watcher.test.mjs proves exact four Git argv and status hash, optional-lock suppression, refusal of failed or unbounded reads, read-only snapshot CLI, bounded summaries and response, Python-compatible ASCII journal, authenticated POST, fake-clock backoff, retry after failure and latest-pending replacement
  known_gap the Bun LaunchAgent was promoted live, but its configured loopback gateway currently has no listener because the existing MCP mesh tunnel is unloaded; no successful live upstream delta is claimed. An ambiguous HTTP failure can cause duplicate remote deltas because the gateway has no idempotency key
  known_gap a porcelain status hash identifies status shape, not content: re-editing an already-dirty tracked file or changing an untracked file without changing its status is not a new delta under the inherited contract

architecture institutional-measurement-surface
  canonical_name InstitutionalMeasurementSurface
  family commands
  domain Commands
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Can an agent operate what this institution measures, or only read about it?
  # The estate grew a dozen organs that measure ceilings, residuals, preservation
  # envelopes and closures, and none of them was reachable through MCP. An agent
  # could read the atlas and could not run anything that produces the numbers the
  # atlas records, so every measurement had exactly one operator: a person at a
  # shell.
  #
  # Adding each as its own tool would have put the estate's vocabulary inside the
  # gateway, which is the hardcoding the namespace work exists to remove. One
  # tool consumes a declaration instead, so a new measurement is a row rather
  # than a release.
  node_types MeasurementSurface
  node_types Receipt
  edge_types runs
  state_types runnable_here
  state_types declared_not_deployed
  invariant which measurements exist is a CMS question and how one is invoked is constrained by the gateway; a runner is a bare filename resolved inside the estate's own script directory, so the registry is content and content cannot choose what executes
  invariant only a read may be run from this surface; an effectful measurement would be a second effect path beside the one the estate governs
  invariant a declared measurement whose runner is not deployed here is listed as not runnable rather than hidden, because hiding it makes a deployment gap look like an absence
  invariant a measurement producing no receipt is an error carrying the runner's own reason, never an empty result
  invariant every measurement carries the bound on how its result may be read, and the bound travels with the response
  forbidden_inference a reachable measurement -> a correct one
  forbidden_inference a measured ceiling -> a promise
  forbidden_inference a computed consequence -> an approval
  computational_form transport
  native_format json
  source_path mcp/rich-native-tools.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_overlay.cue
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/mcp_measure_test.sh
  witness mcp/tests/rich-native-tools.test.mjs proves Python-era runner declarations lower only to present Bun files, effectful and path-shaped declarations are refused, and exact subject flags reach the native runner
