  known_gap the failure cohort reads an operator database that lives on the workstation, so it is declared, deployed and unrunnable on the estate; where a measurement's inputs live is a placement question this surface reports rather than solves
  known_gap the native measurement lowerer has test/contract proof but has not been live promoted; source retirement does not establish live placement
  known_gap a source this entry named could not be opened from this checkout -- /var/lib/bonfyre/cms/content-types/measurement_surface.json. The line is removed rather than repointed to something that merely looks similar, and what remains listed is the evidence this architecture actually stands on.
architecture cmd-interaction-grammar
  canonical_name BonfyreInteractionGrammar
  family command
  domain Command / Interaction grammar
  semantic_question How can a native command bind a reusable donor-informed interaction grammar without turning the donor into a runtime backend or the binding into authority?
  purpose Native command surface for cataloguing twenty market-researched interaction grammars, creating and retiring owner-bound grammar bindings, deriving CreatorChannel and MediaLibrary bindings from active canonical owner rows, rendering an explicitly unverified typed plan and emitting CandidateAdvertisements to the deployed grammar consumer.
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreInteractionGrammar
  internal_calculus catalog | manual binding or current-owner-derived binding -> typed grammar surface plan and AddressPlane advertisement -> consumer -> pending exact-owner composition; public CreatorChannel handoff -> existing Channel surface compiler | retirement -> no advertisement
  invariant a binding's owner reference must match the grammar's catalogued native owner family before the compiler stores it
  forbidden_inference a command output -> an actor-specific exact verifier executed, a right, authority, delivery, payment or effect
  source_path cmd/BonfyreInteractionGrammar/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreInteractionGrammar/tests/interaction_grammar_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreInteractionGrammar/tests/interaction_grammar_test.sh
  source_lineage research/interaction-grammar-market-2026.md
  known_gap external callers must arrive through an authenticated owner-specific binding compiler; raw bind is an internal deterministic owner/compiler operation. Actor-specific target lowerers, including MediaLibrary Listen, remain separately responsible for exact access verification.

architecture organ-drift
  canonical_name OrganDrift
  family command
  domain Command / Which organ a caller actually gets
  layer runtime
  semantic_question When something reaches for a Bonfyre organ, is it running the organ in this tree?
  purpose Most organs exist twice: the build in cmd/, and the managed copy in ~/.bonfyre/bin that the native tool inventory advertises and every MCP invocation runs. This compares their content identities, atomically promotes an explicitly selected managed realization, and receipts the complete managed runtime image.
  maturity measured
  node_types Organ
  node_types ManagedCopy
  edge_types shadows
  internal_calculus divergence is silent by construction. A stale organ does not fail; it does less, and the caller reads the smaller answer as the true one. A promotion copies to a same-directory stage, rehashes it, then renames it atomically; a manifest records every target and digest only after that closure has been checked.
  invariant the check reports before it changes anything; syncing and installing an absent managed realization are separate explicit requests
  invariant a managed runtime image is content-addressed per target; modification time never establishes equivalence
  invariant a failed staged hash leaves the prior managed binary in place and writes no success receipt
  forbidden_inference an organ answering -> the organ in this tree answering
  forbidden_inference a managed binary existing -> it being the current build
  source_path scripts/organ_drift.sh
  source_path scripts/tests/organ_drift_test.sh
  source_path Makefile
  witness 2026-09-25 22 of 98 organs had a managed copy older than the build beside it. bonfyre-embed refused an --input-jsonl flag it had already implemented; bonfyre-vec had no neighbors command and answered a semantic search with zero results that the current build answers correctly; bonfyre-web-address was serving without the identity band compiled into it that same day
  witness 2026-09-25 after syncing, the same query -- "flooding and climate damage in south asia" over 790 real ONNX embeddings -- returned "How two elections reshaped the India-Bangladesh border" and "Environmental and Economic Impacts of Super El Nino" through the managed path the MCP uses
  witness 2026-09-26 scripts/tests/organ_drift_test.sh proves an inspection does not mutate a stale carrier, an FPQ target spelling is taken from its Makefile rather than guessed from PascalCase, a digest-verified stage atomically promotes the target, verify refuses later drift without repairing it, and an absent managed organ is installed only with the separate --install-missing request
  witness 2026-09-26 ~/.bonfyre/bin/.bonfyre-organ-manifest.json records a digest-verified 123-organ local runtime image: the first closure found 72 stale and 35 absent managed realizations; after explicit promotion/install and a final race-catching verify, 123 are current with zero stale, missing, or refused realizations
  known_gap nothing rebuilds or compares these on a schedule; the drift is found only when someone runs the check or trips over an organ doing less than it should
  known_gap byte identity proves the managed carrier equals this checkout build, not that the build's semantic contracts, library dependencies, service environment, or remote deployment are healthy

