architecture cmd-books
  canonical_name BonfyreBooks
  family command
  domain Command / CheapCognition
  semantic_question Which of the client's accounts does each bank or card line belong to, decided on this machine, and which lines must a person look at?
  purpose Bookkeeping categorisation that never sends a client's transactions anywhere: weights learned from the client's own history answer first, a local model takes what they are unsure of
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreBooks
  internal_calculus bonfyre-books (C, cmd/BonfyreDecide; one program for the three products) over libbonfyre bf_jv/bf_jsonw/bf_re; ledger_category in decision-plane.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/books.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/books_xlsx.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/dp_core.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/Makefile
  internal_calculus XLSX exchange in C (cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/books_xlsx.c): bounded compressed and expanded ZIP members read with zlib, SheetJS-equivalent cell, date and range reading, explicit worksheet and header selection, exact source cell identities, and a formula-bearing review workbook written over existing Books decisions
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh replays the vectors recorded from the retired books-workbook.test.mjs programs, which exercised real XLSX bytes through the existing Books CLI, retained source hashes and cells, unknown amounts, hidden rows, formula-cache refusal, malformed archives, input preservation and formula-bearing output without loading a model; the C build reproduces them byte for byte (47 vectors, 2026-10-22)
  invariant workbook input retains its original bytes and SHA-256; imported rows retain actual sheet and cell coordinates even when blank rows are skipped; a review export cannot overwrite an input file through the CLI
  invariant mapped formula and error cells refuse import instead of treating an unverified cached result as financial evidence; input limits are 8 MiB compressed, 32 MiB expanded and 200000 selected cells
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-calculation.test.mjs independently recalculates exported Books formulas with Univer and verifies edited assumptions after XLSX export and reopen
  interacts books-review-enters-financial-workbook
  known_gap the financial-workbook owner implements editing and native destination retention with isolated calculation and account tests; visual browser inspection, live installation and reviewed ledger posting remain unverified or unimplemented
  forbidden_inference an XLSX review export or cached formula result -> a reconciled account, verified recalculation, approved journal or tested browser experience
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh replays the vectors recorded from the retired products.test.mjs programs, which proved confident lines are answered by the learned owner without asking the model, an unseen merchant goes to the local model, and the given accounts are scored; the C build reproduces them byte for byte (47 vectors, 2026-10-22)
  witness packs/no-simulation/aurekai-products-20261016/books-september.json on 1,500 held-out lines of DoDataThings/us-bank-transaction-categories-v2 (public, synthetic, MIT) after learning the first 6,000: 1,476 booked, 1,460 right, 24 held for review
  witness packs/no-simulation/aurekai-products-20261016/books-cold-start.csv with no history, 31 of 40 hand-written Schedule C lines suggested right by coder-7B, all held for review; 3B models suggested 17 to 24
  invariant the learned owner is a pinned weight file whose SHA-256 is the receipt's artifact; a line it answers below 0.7 is asked of the local model with the client's most similar earlier lines
  invariant with no learned history every line is held for review
  invariant transactions are information_policy private and never reach a hosted provider
  forbidden_inference a booked line -> a reviewed ledger
  forbidden_inference accuracy on a public synthetic set -> accuracy on a particular client's books
  known_gap a merchant rule from history covered 59% of held-out lines at 93.6% and is not used; real bank exports with real merchants were not available to measure
  invariant amounts are read exactly in integer cents ($1,234.56, -12.50, (12.50), 12.50-, CR/DR); an empty or unreadable cell is unresolved, kept as written, and its line held, never booked as zero
  invariant columns are resolved by exact header first; two candidates for one role, or a signed amount beside debit/credit columns, refuses the import until --columns names them; Debit Amount and Credit Amount are debit and credit, not amount
  invariant a learned answer books only at confidence 0.7 or more and when ledger_category's own selection (expected loss of a wrong booking against review cost, review probability, risk ties) chooses it; lowering the escalation line cannot override that selection; a local-model answer is a suggestion held for review, because its probabilities are not calibrated against the client's books
  invariant each line's mask digest is its own date, description and amount text under the chart, the learned artifact and the resolved column mapping, so an added line leaves every other line's case and a retained deterministic answer unchanged; identical lines stay separate subjects
  invariant unsure lines read history through token postings built once per run, ranked by the same Jaccard score with ties in history order as the full scan
  invariant amounts are checked exactly (BigInt) before becoming integer cents and totals are summed exactly; an amount or total past exact range is unresolved or refused, never rounded; an unterminated quoted field, a header name used twice and two roles given one column refuse the import; money on both debit and credit of one line is held, not netted; an unnamed spacer column never holds a role
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh replays the vectors recorded from the retired products.test.mjs programs, which proved postings ranking equals the full scan with ties, row-scoped masks with reuse of an unchanged line by the retained learned owner, the import safeguards above, and a 0.72 learned answer held by the selection with escalateBelow lowered to 0.1 (12 tests, 2026-10-17); the C build reproduces them byte for byte (47 vectors, 2026-10-22)
  witness 2026-10-17 on the same 1,500 held-out lines, learned only: the selection holds 2 more lines (both right), 1,445 booked at 99.4%; the 53 unsure lines read 6,000 earlier lines in 179 ms through postings against 2,163 ms by full scan, identical results
  invariant history is searched and the model acquired only for the lines still unsure after the learned weights; a model that cannot be admitted leaves the learned results intact and every unsure line held
  witness packs/no-simulation/aurekai-products-20261017/books-september-learned-only.json on the same 1,500 held-out lines with no model admitted: 1,447 booked by the learned weights, 1,438 right (99.4%), 53 held for review, 0.6 s
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh replays the vectors recorded from the retired products.test.mjs programs, which proved exact amount parsing, unresolved empty and unreadable cells, debit/credit columns, refusal of ambiguous imports, a model suggestion held for review, and a settled run that never acquires a model (2026-10-17); the C build reproduces them byte for byte (47 vectors, 2026-10-22)
  known_gap the 2026-10-16 witness (1,476 booked, 1,460 right) let model answers book lines; that is no longer the contract, and model suggestion quality under the new forced-continuation scoring has not been re-measured
  invariant installed by make -C cmd/BonfyreDecide install as one C program (246 KB, replacing three 63 MB bun-compiled executables) hard-linked as bonfyre-books, bonfyre-monitor and bonfyre-manifest in ~/.bonfyre/bin, with the DecisionPlane CUE export compiled in as data, so it runs without the checkout or the cue tool and MCP native discovery classifies it as a Mach-O native executable
  witness 2026-10-17: MCP native_tool_invoke ran the installed binary end to end (BonfyreBooks on the 1,500 held-out lines: 1,447 booked, 1,438 right, 1.2 s round trip; BonfyreMonitor reached the model front and returned its admission refusal); before, all three were refused as interpreter launchers
  forbidden_inference an installed binary -> the current source; it is as fresh as its last make -C cmd/BonfyreDecide install
  invariant XLSX text is XML-unescaped once, as OOXML specifies; SheetJS 0.20.3 decoded inline string cells twice and turned a literal "&amp;" into "&" (cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/CORRECTIONS)
  forbidden_inference golden-vector parity with the retired Bun programs -> correctness of their behaviour; the vectors fix what they did, mistakes included, except the listed corrections

architecture cmd-manifest
  canonical_name BonfyreManifest
  family command
  domain Command / CheapCognition
  semantic_question What does a seller's equipment lot contain, as far as its photos and listing state it, and what must be confirmed before a buyer prices it?
  purpose An itemised manifest from what a seller already gave; buyers discount lots without one
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreManifest
  internal_calculus bonfyre-manifest (C, cmd/BonfyreDecide; one program for the three products) over libbonfyre bf_jv/bf_jsonw/bf_re and manifest_unit in decision-plane.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/manifest.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/dp_core.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/dp_gguf.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/Makefile
  source_path cmd/BonfyreOCR/src/main.swift
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh replays the vectors recorded from the retired products.test.mjs programs, which proved exact brand, family (OCR-truncated ELITEDES is EliteDesk), part number and count; toner settled as a consumable by its own words; a computer data-bearing; the ITAD Exchange import columns; the C build reproduces them byte for byte (47 vectors, 2026-10-22)
  witness packs/no-simulation/aurekai-products-20261016/manifest-wholesale.json on seven real lots from the 2026-10-09 wholesale pipeline (Craigslist photos and two retained listings): HP EliteDesk desktop, Vertiv cable manager, a 121-unit toner lot and a mixed computer store read; one photo with no text and one brand-only photo asked for confirmation; a Dell toner photo was wrongly called a desktop
  invariant brand, model family, part number, quantity and the listing's own condition and make are copied from text, never generated
  invariant a unit with no readable words is not asked about; a brand-only unit gets no kind; text with no condition words is condition unknown
  forbidden_inference a manifest from photos and a listing -> units counted, tested or owned
  known_gap 600x450 marketplace photos rarely show a label; most lots need the listing text or label photos to be itemised
  invariant the ITAD file prices qty units, so a unit whose count was not stated, that was never read, or whose kind is unknown is held in FILE.held.tsv with its reason, never exported as one
  invariant supplies settle the kind exactly only when the text names no equipment beside them; a 42U rack with servers and drives is asked about, not called supplies
  invariant a count is never a model number: the family match (OptiPlex 7050) is removed before a count is read; a maker read from the family is make_by model family, kept apart from a stated brand
  witness packs/no-simulation/aurekai-products-20261017/manifest-wholesale-itad.tsv replays the seven 2026-10-16 wholesale lots: the old ITAD file priced five uncounted lots at qty 1; now only the toner lot with its stated 121 is exported and six are held with their reasons (manifest-wholesale-itad.held.tsv)
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh replays the vectors recorded from the retired products.test.mjs programs, which proved the uncounted OptiPlex lot is held, not priced as 7,050 or as one, and a 42U rack with servers is not supplies (2026-10-17); the C build reproduces them byte for byte (47 vectors, 2026-10-22)
  known_gap OCR resolves the installed ~/.bonfyre/bin/bonfyre-ocr, then PATH, then a checkout build; the lot is still a set of files, not a reviewed inventory record two people can reconcile
  invariant installed by make -C cmd/BonfyreDecide install as one C program (246 KB, replacing three 63 MB bun-compiled executables) hard-linked as bonfyre-books, bonfyre-monitor and bonfyre-manifest in ~/.bonfyre/bin, with the DecisionPlane CUE export compiled in as data, so it runs without the checkout or the cue tool and MCP native discovery classifies it as a Mach-O native executable
  witness 2026-10-17: MCP native_tool_invoke ran the installed binary end to end (BonfyreBooks on the 1,500 held-out lines: 1,447 booked, 1,438 right, 1.2 s round trip; BonfyreMonitor reached the model front and returned its admission refusal); before, all three were refused as interpreter launchers
  forbidden_inference an installed binary -> the current source; it is as fresh as its last make -C cmd/BonfyreDecide install

interaction surface-maturity-lake-check-feeds-live-sweep
  source cmd-surface-maturity
  destination web-address-edge
  relation reports_lake_regressions
  preserves each regression's metric, its floor and its current value, folded into one subject-lake goal per estate
  drops coverage that held and every metric the floor does not name
  forbidden_inference a lake goal -> a repair, a rollout or a write to any owner store; the sweep only records the defect
  invalidates_on CMS publisher identity, the subject fabric's bundles and readers, the item archive, the frontier ledger
  witness scripts/tests/live_sweep_lake_test.sh

interaction cited-brief-reads-foreign-twin-receipts
  source cmd-brief
  destination foreign-twin
  relation reads
  preserves the receipt's twin, observed time, policy decision and content sha256, and the retained body bytes, as the only material a cited brief may quote
  drops any path by which a brief could fetch, refresh or re-observe a source, or cite a body whose hash no longer matches its receipt
  forbidden_inference a brief quoting a receipt-bound body -> the source is current, correct or licensed for reuse
  witness cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/cited_brief_test.sh refuses a deny-policy receipt for the same twin and drops a body changed after its receipt
  binding cmd/BonfyreBrief/src/cited.c

interaction practice-intake-becomes-brief-inventory
  source cmd-brief
  destination service-site
  relation reads
  preserves the answers one request left through the practice site's offer form, keyed by the brief type's fact names, with the request reference, received time and inbox sha256
  drops the requester's name, contact and message text, and any answer to a count that is not a plain number
  forbidden_inference an inventory built from intake answers -> the account holds what the person said, or authority to read their server
  witness cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/hosting_inventory_test.sh reads the inbox fixture, and with BONFYRE_TEST_WEB_BINARY the practice draft's own form and site inbox --json
  binding cmd/BonfyreBrief/src/inventory.c

interaction cited-brief-output-reaches-account-outputs
  source cmd-brief
  destination cmd-queue
  relation projects
  preserves the brief file as the output_uri of a completed WorkGraph job, which the existing account-work index projects into that account's Work and Outputs
  drops any path by which writing a brief admits work, assigns a task or appears under an account whose index does not read that WorkGraph
  forbidden_inference a brief listed in Outputs -> an accepted deliverable, reviewed criteria or work the customer authorized
  witness cmd/BonfyreBrief/tests/cited_brief_test.sh enqueues, claims and acks one job naming brief.md and reads it back from account-work outputs for user:7, absent for user:8
  binding cmd/BonfyreQueue/src/account_work.h

interaction embed-static-store-feeds-physics-pack
  source cmd-embed
  destination cmd-physics
  relation admitted-static-vectors-become-hamiltonian-field
  preserves the .bfse sha256, corpus sha256, every visible vector as float32 at the model's width, and the store key sha256(schema, model digest, text) through embed pack into a .bfpack that bvh, init --pack-row, run and energy read
  drops passage ids and text, invisible rows, the teacher, the agreement score as a quality claim, and any authority to publish or act on a trajectory
  forbidden_inference a pack built from the static store -> retrieval quality, teacher geometry, or a meaningful trajectory; only the integrator's conservation is witnessed over it
  invalidates_on .bfse bytes, corpus bytes, store key schema, pack format or physics potential change
  witness cmd/BonfyrePhysics/tests/real_vector_witness_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreEmbed/src/static_embed.h

interaction workgraph-run-evidence-projects-to-account-work
  source work-graph
  destination cmd-queue
  relation projects
  preserves the claimed attempt's attested harness, provider session id, recorded handoff digest and the attempt's own outcome, read from the node's chained run_attested receipt through a read-only ATTACH
  drops unattested attempts as runs, receipts whose harness, session or handoff is malformed, and any join by time, title or worker name
  binding cmd/BonfyreQueue/src/account_work.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreQueue/tests/account_work_index_test.sh
  forbidden_inference a projected governed run -> provider usage, cost or quality

interaction account-work-governed-runs-feed-meter-context-compare
  source cmd-queue
  destination cmd-meter
  relation reads_through
  preserves the exact provider session as the only usage join key and the run's recorded handoff_ref as the handoff binding
  drops a caller's declaration where the governed attempt recorded a different handoff, and a baseline run that recorded the compared handoff
  binding cmd/BonfyreMeter/src/meter_context.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/context_compare_test.sh
  forbidden_inference a recorded handoff binding -> the agent consumed the handoff or the delta was caused by it

architecture cmd-obsidian
  canonical_name BonfyreObsidian
  family command
  domain Command / Obsidian
  semantic_question What does the BonfyreObsidian capability organ realize, and by what contract?
  purpose Command-surface organ realizing ObsidianVaultBinding: account-scoped Obsidian vaults read, written and synced through the desktop CLI, Obsidian Headless or the files. Its contract is cmd/BonfyreObsidian/README.md.
  maturity implemented
  command BonfyreObsidian
  internal_calculus bonfyre-obsidian binary
  interacts obsidian-vault-binding
  forbidden_inference the command exists -> its effect is authorized; Authority gates mutation and read scope still applies
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/vault.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/drive.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/Makefile
  witness cmd/BonfyreObsidian/tests/obsidian_test.sh
  source_lineage authored with the organ on 2026-10-31
  known_gap built in cmd only, not installed to ~/.bonfyre/bin; no caller wires it into a web route, MCP tool or flow yet
